// Viewer response for year-folder media: what browsers are told when the
// origin says nothing. The bucket's objects carry no Cache-Control, so without
// this browsers fall back to their own heuristics.
//
// A response that already has a Cache-Control keeps it: the instance's own
// lifetime for a file the sync has not copied yet. And only successful
// responses get here. CloudFront does not run viewer response functions for
// status 400 or above, so an error - both origins failing during an instance
// replacement, say - is never marked cacheable. A response headers policy
// would have been simpler, and would have added the header to those errors.
//
// It does not change how long CloudFront keeps the file, which is
// CachingOptimized's day.

function handler(event) {
    var response = event.response;

    if (!response.headers['cache-control']) {
        response.headers['cache-control'] = { value: 'public, max-age=${ttl}' };
    }

    return response;
}
